# Rust
target/
# Cargo.lock is intentionally tracked (not ignored) for fixtures/ — a
# benchmark run should be fully reproducible, same as npm/deno lockfiles.

# Swift
.build/
.swiftpm/

# Node / Deno
node_modules/
.deno/

# scratch run dirs, if ever created under the repo instead of /tmp
runner/runs/

# DFlash2 llama.cpp fork checkout + build (runner/setup_dflash2_fork.sh) —
# a full llama.cpp source tree + compiled binary, too large/volatile to
# commit; the setup script is what's durable, not this output.
runner/.dflash2-fork/

# Mainline llama.cpp checkout + build, built at HEAD for DSpark support
# ahead of the Homebrew bottle (runner/setup_dspark_head.sh) — same reason
# as .dflash2-fork/ above.
runner/.dspark-head/

# Python bytecode cache
runner/__pycache__/

# Durable per-task JSON results for the PROMPT suites (sanity/hermes_ops),
# added by the H-4 fix — added 2026-08-21 (3rd adversarial review, low
# finding). Unlike results/transcripts/ (coding suites, explicitly
# committed forever per AGENTS.md — each one is a unique, non-reproducible
# agentic transcript worth keeping), these duplicate information already
# in results/log.jsonl (pass/fail, tokens, timing, grade_output) in a more
# verbose form, and prompt-suite tasks run far more often per sweep
# (every sanity/hermes_ops task × every trial × every model, on every
# invocation, not just the interesting coding-suite paths) — left
# untracked, local-only, so a big --trials sweep doesn't bloat git
# history. Kept on disk for local investigation; not committed.
results/prompt_results/
